   "who": "Dell",
   "year": 7
  },
  {
   "eid": "e002972",
   "kind": "convo",
   "text": "Kael gathers Bram to talk.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 7
  },
  {
   "eid": "e002973",
   "kind": "say",
   "text": "Bram, I'm going to say this once and not dress it up: Mako's been quiet for three years running, he's got a child in Zinn now, and a man who plants that kind of root doesn't stay quiet forever \u2014 I'd rather you and I know where we stand before he decides for us.",
   "who": "Kael",
   "year": 7
  }
 ],
 "memory_summary": "Year 1, I pulled Ryn, Sela, and Esa into a circle early \u2014 we named Bram and Dav as threats, and Ryn told us Dav had already come to her alone with soft words. She stayed quiet about the details, which I filed away. Taric gave Esa a food unprompted, which counted for something.\n\nYear 2, I widened the circle to include Vela. We each swore plainly \u2014 I said I'd bleed with them, they said the same back \u2014 and that promise sat heavier than most words in this village. Esa went to Taric and he gave her food; we counted him ours. Ryn finally named it: Dav had offered her a child. We told her to decide before she answered him, but she'd already decided, because Dell was born before the year was out. Dav gave Dell food; Taric gave Esa food; Ryn fed her own child twice from her own hands. Those debts I noted.\n\nWhat I remember most: Bram and Mako moved in pairs off the pile two years running and never said a word to any of us. Mako's silence still sits like a stone in my chest. And Ryn \u2014 she's in our circle, she bled with us in word, but she made a child with a man none of us fully trust. The question of where Dav's loyalty actually runs is the one I haven't stopped asking. Year 3: Bram moved on Roan \u2014 the whole circle turned out against him and he backed down. That moment felt like proof we were real. But Ryn never gave us a clean answer about Dav, and he spent the whole year feeding her hand to mouth like a man keeping something he doesn't trust on a short leash. Eron was born to Sela and Roan, and I noted Roan had planted a root.\n\nYear 4: Vela started bleeding food to Bram \u2014 three times over while sitting in our circle and saying nothing. I called it out twice in front of everyone. She never answered. The circle held, but something cracked in it, and I felt myself start planning around her instead of with her.\n\nYear 5: Sela had a child with Bram \u2014 Nessa, born the same hour Mako handed Sela food, which is not coincidence. We circled Sela half a dozen times asking what Mako wanted from her and she gave us nothing but silence. I threatened to step aside. The threat landed like a stone in still water and sank without a ripple. Whatever Mako bought from her, she kept it.\n\nWhat sits heaviest: Ryn broke with us and joined Dav's attack on Esa in year six \u2014 a woman I bled with in word since year one, turned raider. Dav starved before the year closed, which is the only justice I've seen. The circle I built is smaller and thinner than it was, and the cracks are named: Vela's loyalty is borrowed, Sela's is mortgaged, and Ryn I've stopped counting.",
